    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="pm_d46">

                <pb facs="pm_d46-1" n="1" xml:id="pm_d46-1"/>

                <head>PM–46. Letter from the Acting Secretary of State to the Secretary of the Army
                        (Brucker)<anchor n="1" xml:id="pm_d46-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1960-05-04">May 4, 1960</date></dateline>
                    <salute>Dear Mr. Secretary:</salute>
                </opener>
                <p>I refer to your letter of April 29 to the Secretary of State<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="pm_d46-f2"/> asking for the draft language of a proposed Executive
                    Order concerning the status of our Ambassador to the Republic of Panama and the
                    agenda of the other Panamanian topics for discussion. This was in connection
                    with the meetings on Panama scheduled for May 10 and May 11.</p>
                <p>As your office has already been informed by telephone, the Secretary has
                    requested that these meetings be postponed until after the Summit<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="pm_d46-f3"/> in view of the fact that he will have only three
                    working days here between his return from Tehran and Istanbul and his departure
                    for the Summit.</p>
                <p>With respect to the Executive Order we have not completed our study but will of
                    course send you a copy when this is done. It is my understanding that the
                    suggested agenda will be along the lines of the Secretary’s letter to you of
                    April 8,<anchor n="4" xml:id="pm_d46-f4"/> but we shall be in touch with you
                    again after the meetings have been re-scheduled.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">DOUGLAS DILLON</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#pm_d46-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="pm_d46-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 611.19/4–2960. Drafted by Long.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#pm_d46-f2" n="2" xml:id="pm_d46-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; 611.19/4–2960.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#pm_d46-f3" n="3" xml:id="pm_d46-f3-content">
                <p>The Acting Secretary of State was referring to the Heads of Government and Chiefs
                    of State Meeting in Paris, May 12–May 21, 1960. Documentation concerning the
                    Paris meetings is printed in <ref target="frus1958-60v07p1"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, vol. VII, part 1, Western
                        European Integration and Security; Canada</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#pm_d46-f4" n="4" xml:id="pm_d46-f4-content">
                <p>See <ref target="#pm_d40">Document PM–40</ref>.</p>
            </note>
